      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:4:2:27:3",
      "text": [
        " الَّذِي يَذْرَعُهُ الْقَيْ‏ءُ وَ هُوَ صَائِمٌ قَالَ يُتِمُّ صَوْمَهُ وَ لَا يَقْضِي ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Ismail, from Al Fazl Bin ShAzan, from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Muawiya, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> regarding the one who nauseates to vomit (but does not), and he is Fasting. He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘Let him complete his Fast and the does not have to make up for it’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "3. Muhammad ibn ‘Isma‘il has narrated from al-Fadl ibn Shadhan, from ibn abu ‘Umayr, from Mu‘awiyah who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘One who feels like vomiting must complete his fast and there is no Qada’ (compensatory fast) on him.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
